FIX-94 got the movers ranked (95) and picked (AKE, DRV, SAGA, G, PUMP, SUI). tape/universe.js then re-verifies
each nominee against the venue and refuses anything under config.wideeye.nominationFloorUsd before the hot lane
may adopt it. At $2,000,000 a day that refused almost every runner the watch had just picked.

Of the 77 Kraken USD pairs that ran >= 10% from the open on 2026-09-20, the liquid ones traded $180k-$264k a
DAY (CTSI $192k, GNOT $228k, LAPTOP $264k, B2 $180k, MYX $220k); only DRV ($2.06M) could clear $2M.

wideeye.nominationFloorUsd 2_000_000 -> 100_000 — the same line the runners study used for 'tradable at $500
without moving the book' ($500 is 0.5% of a day's flow). ONE config value, audited in the SCOPE-5 config fence.

Bounds unchanged: hot lane still 6 slots / 2 h tenure; deep universe still capped at 30 by volume (hot-lane
verification runs against the UNCAPPED relaxed list, so an adopted runner is not then shed — checked); the
Judge's frozen book-depth, protective-exit-at-depth and cost law on the live book remains the real gate. Dust
stays out: SYND $9k/day, DUCK $2k, BLUE $1k are refused.

Tests: publish-fix-94-watch-sees-runners 7/7 (FIX95-1 pins the real volumes and shows only DRV survived the old
floor). wideeye 6/6 (below-floor fixture moved to $50k). Green: social-4f-scope 9, universe 9, tape-hot-lane 4,
paper-runtime 8, judge-composition 4.

